I've made a complete mess of CD images for Beta2 so far as the result of a=
=20
wrong assumption. This means, as some installation reports and comments=20
have shown, that CD images linked from [1] have been broken since last=20
=46riday.

The good news is that there are now good Beta2 netinst and businesscard CD=
=20
test images available from [1]. Note that these are not the regular=20
etch_d-i or sid_d-i. The correct link for Beta2 images is currently:
http://cdimage.debian.org/cdimage/beta2-test-build/

Initial tests using these images for i386 and sparc64 have shown no=20
problems. Tests for other arches are very much appreciated [2].

This also means that there are no good full CD images available yet.=20
However, some issues with full CD images have been identified [3] and are=20
being worked on.


I've also uploaded the (hopefully final) 20060302 build of=20
debian-installer today which includes the new 2.6.15-7 kernels. It has=20
been accepted for i386 and so should now start building for all arches.

We will probably have a small further delay in the Beta2 release, but=20
because no blocking issues have been identified as yet, it looks as if we=20
can keep it minimal. I'm somewhat reluctant to post hard dates ATM.

I'm very sorry for any confusion. Please blame it on my inexperience as=20
release manager for d-i and the complexity of the whole process.

Cheers,
=46JP

[1] http://www.debian.org/devel/debian-installer/
[2] SVN: installer/doc/devel/release-checklist
[3] http://lists.debian.org/debian-boot/2006/03/msg00050.html

