Hi,

I have a simple SATA card: 0000:00:07.0 RAID bus controller: Silicon 
Image, Inc. SiI 3114 Serial ATA Controller (rev 02) - It is NOT RAID, 
this is because Silicon Image wants to sell them as RAID, but its 
only a Windows-Driver-Soft-RAID, so Linux sees on x86 and Alpha 4 
SATA ports. I am running a Seagate Barracuda 7200rpm 120 GB disk on it.
Works without any problems. This one costs about 15 Euros and it's 
32bit. If you want faster performance choose a 64 bit one, but for 
alpha machines this is not needed because 35 MB/sec IO is the maximum 
I get from this card with current discs and the mainboard/processor 
and it is 3 times faster than SCSI in this machine :)

Uwe

